## Check cloud-init

The nodes have finished booting, and with that cloud-init's final stage, which
writes the munge key and runs the `runcmd` restarts. Check that it succeeded
on every node: exit status 2 means it finished with recoverable errors, which
any `cc_*` module warning produces, and lets the node through. `$?` and `$rc`
are escaped so that the compute node expands them rather than the head node.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Check that cloud-init succeeded on the compute nodes -->
```bash
pdsh -S -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" \
	"cloud-init status >/dev/null; rc=\$?; [ \$rc -eq 0 ] || [ \$rc -eq 2 ]" \
	|| { echo "cloud-init: FAILED; check podman logs cloud-init-server"; exit 1; }
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

If IPoIB is configured, continue after it is up on every compute node:
NetworkManager activates each node's connection once the interface and its
InfiniBand link appear. To check one node:

```bash
ssh ${compute_prefix}1 nmcli -g GENERAL.STATE connection show ${ipoib_dev}
```

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_ipoib -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Wait for IPoIB on the compute nodes -->
<!-- ohpc_command for ((t=0; ; t++)) ; do -->
<!-- ohpc_command     pdsh -S -w "${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" \ -->
<!-- ohpc_command         "nmcli -g GENERAL.STATE connection show ${ipoib_dev} | grep -qx activated" \ -->
<!-- ohpc_command         >/dev/null 2>&1 && { echo "compute IPoIB: OK"; break; } -->
<!-- ohpc_command     (( t < 30 )) || { echo "compute IPoIB: FAILED"; exit 1; } -->
<!-- ohpc_command     echo "Waiting for IPoIB on the compute nodes..." -->
<!-- ohpc_command     sleep 10 -->
<!-- ohpc_command done -->
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
